{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ywg2huq755lm5yeoq2fcbrsm25gilxkzrbcq7pfvlhfzvswlrdsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\nA single exported C function: `void colourblind(cb_impairment, float*, float*, float*)` — a 3×3 float matrix multiply selected by a 3-value enum. The three transform helpers are `static` in C, so `colourblind` is the entire ABI.\n\n## Bug found and fixed\n**Debug-profile abort on misaligned pointers.** The Rust used `*red` / `*red = …` on `*mut f32`, which carries an alignment precondition that Rust checks in debug builds:\n\n```\npanicked at src/lib.rs:130: misaligned pointer dereference:\naddress must be a multiple of 0x4 but is 0x7f955a1f42c1\nthread caused non-unwinding panic. aborting.\n```\n\nThe C compiles `*Red` to a plain `movss`, which has no alignment requirement, so the C serves an under-aligned `float*` normally. Fixed by switching the 3 loads and 9 stores to `read_unaligned`/`write_unaligned` — identical `movss` codegen, no debug abort. Debug now passes 11/11 error tests where it previously aborted.\n\n## Results\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `nm -D` symbol diff | **empty** — `colourblind` exported by both; C statics correctly unexported; no unresolved non-libc symbols |\n| Phase B — 24 `CONFIGS.md` rows | **all pass** (25 tests) |\n| Phase C — 8 `ERRORS.md` rows + 4 boundary rows | **all pass** (11 tests) |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — no `[[bin]]`, no `main()` |\n| Feature combos × profiles | 4/4 green (`default`/`--no-default-features` × release/debug) |\n\n## Harness sensitivity proven, not assumed\n`mutation_check.sh` builds 8 deliberately-broken Rust variants; **all 8 are killed**, including the subtlest — flipping one `addss` operand order, which changes *only* NaN payload selection (caught by `cfg_c12`/`cfg_c13`). Notably `cfg_c14` (10k random bit patterns) missed that one, confirming the dedicated multi-NaN rows are load-bearing.\n\n## One thing to flag\nThe Rust matches the C **as its own build system builds it** (`flags.make` is literally `C_FLAGS = -fPIC` → gcc `-O0`): 0 failures. Rebuilt at `-O1`/`-O2`/`-O3`/`-Os`, the same C source diverges on 3 NaN tests — but it diverges *from itself*, because gcc reorders operands at `-O1`+ and `ADDSS` returns the destination NaN. No single implementation can match both builds; the translation is pinned to the canonical one. All non-NaN inputs agree across all five C builds. Documented in `CONFIGS.md` and printed by `run_all.sh`.\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `tests/{common,phase_b_configs,phase_c_errors,phase_d_symbols}`, `run_all.sh`, `mutation_check.sh`. `c_src/` unmodified. Note that `cargo` needs `--offline` here (crates.io is proxy-blocked; `libloading 0.8.9` was in the local cache)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":862,"cache_read_input_tokens":95934,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":862,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3136d9f-f282-422f-9b07-dc139c105824","uuid":"f14da0e8-6419-4e5b-a84c-27bc6de3b406","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:59:09.677Z"}
